      { heading: "Building Your First Product", content: "The best approach for student founders is to start with free tools and only upgrade when free tiers genuinely limit your growth. Many successful startups were built entirely on free tools in their early stages.\n\nHere's a recommended free stack for a student startup: EPIC for design and branding, GitHub for code, Vercel for hosting, Supabase for backend, Notion for documentation, and Google Analytics for tracking.\n\nFocus on building your product and finding customers before spending money on tools. A startup's success is determined by product-market fit, not by how premium your tools are.\n\nUse EPIC's navigation maker to plan your product's page structure before building. This 30-minute planning exercise can save weeks of development time and ensure you build the right features in the right order." }
